# Authors

This project was built by three collaborators, contributing equally.

## Authors

**Alex Borwick**

**Jaspreet Singh** — [@jas9x9](https://github.com/jas9x9)

**Seti Arabshahi** — [@0Seti0](https://github.com/0Seti0)

## How we came together

This work began during the [LISA AI Studio] 2026 cohort — a programme run by the London Initiative for Safe AI for professionals exploring AI safety. The three of us were participants in the cohort.

## Acknowledgements

We're grateful to:

- **The LISA AI Studio team**, for the structure, the programme, and the conversations that shaped this work.
- **The interview participants** who shared their pivot stories, frustrations, and questions during the research phase. Their experiences are the foundation of these skills.
- **Field-building organisations and individuals** working on AI safety career infrastructure, whose published guidance and resources we drew on extensively. Where specific sources are referenced in the skills, they are linked in the relevant `references/` directories.

## Contact

For project-related questions, please [open an issue](https://github.com/ais-skills-collective/ais-skills-for-generalists/issues) on this repository.
